{
    "cells": [
        {
            "cell_type": "markdown",
            "metadata": {},
            "source": [
                "# Tutorial 1: Basic Usage of Reltrans\n",
                "\n",
                "This tutorial demonstrates how to load the `reltrans` compiled library and run the model to generate spectra.\n",
                "We will also explore how the spectrum changes when varying key parameters like **Spin** and **Inclination**."
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "code",
            "execution_count": null,
            "metadata": {},
            "outputs": [],
            "source": [
                "import os\n",
                "import sys\n",
                "import ctypes as ct\n",
                "import numpy as np\n",
                "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
                "\n",
                "%matplotlib inline"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "markdown",
            "metadata": {},
            "source": [
                "## 1. Load the Compiled Library\n",
                "\n",
                "We need to load the `libreltrans.so` (Linux) or `libreltrans.dylib` (macOS) shared library.\n",
                "Ensure you have compiled the code using `make` before running this notebook.\n",
                "\n",
                "> **Note:** If you are running this in an environment without the compiled library, the cells below will fail."
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "code",
            "execution_count": null,
            "metadata": {},
            "outputs": [],
            "source": [
                "# Try to locate the library in the build directory\n",
                "lib_path = os.path.abspath(os.path.join(os.getcwd(), '../build/lib/libreltrans.so'))\n",
                "\n",
                "if not os.path.exists(lib_path):\n",
                "    # Try MacOS extension\n",
                "    lib_path = os.path.abspath(os.path.join(os.getcwd(), '../build/lib/libreltrans.dylib'))\n",
                "\n",
                "if not os.path.exists(lib_path):\n",
                "    print(f\"Warning: Library not found at {lib_path}. Please compile reltrans first.\")\n",
                "    # Depending on your setup, you might need to adjust the path above\n",
                "    lib = None\n",
                "else:\n",
                "    print(f\"Loading library from {lib_path}\")\n",
                "    lib = ct.cdll.LoadLibrary(lib_path)"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "markdown",
            "metadata": {},
            "source": [
                "## 2. Define the Interface\n",
                "\n",
                "We define the function signatures to match the Fortran subroutines.  \n",
                "Here we focus on `tdreltransPL`, which calculates the transfer function for a Power Law illumination.\n",
                "\n",
                "**Subroutine Signature:**\n",
                "`subroutine tdreltransPL(ear, ne, param, ifl, photar)`"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "code",
            "execution_count": null,
            "metadata": {},
            "outputs": [],
            "source": [
                "if lib:\n",
                "    # Define Ctypes pointer types\n",
                "    type_float_p = ct.POINTER(ct.c_float)\n",
                "    type_int_p   = ct.POINTER(ct.c_int)\n",
                "\n",
                "    # Get the function from the library\n",
                "    # Note: Fortran compilers often append an underscore to function names\n",
                "    try:\n",
                "        reltrans_pl_func = lib.tdreltranspl_\n",
                "        reltrans_pl_func.argtypes = [type_float_p, type_int_p, type_float_p, type_int_p, type_float_p]\n",
                "        reltrans_pl_func.restype  = None\n",
                "        print(\"Function 'tdreltranspl_' loaded successfully.\")\n",
                "    except AttributeError:\n",
                "        print(\"Error: Could not find 'tdreltranspl_' in the library.\")\n",
                "        lib = None"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "code",
            "execution_count": null,
            "metadata": {},
            "outputs": [],
            "source": [
                "def run_reltrans_pl(energy_edges, params):\n",
                "    \"\"\"\n",
                "    Wrapper to call the Fortran tdreltransPL subroutine.\n",
                "    \n",
                "    Args:\n",
                "        energy_edges (np.array): Energy bin edges (keV).\n",
                "        params (np.array): Model parameters.\n",
                "        \n",
                "    Returns:\n",
                "        np.array: Photon flux in each bin.\n",
                "    \"\"\"\n",
                "    if lib is None:\n",
                "        raise ImportError(\"Reltrans library not loaded.\")\n",
                "\n",
                "    ne = len(energy_edges) - 1\n",
                "    photar = np.zeros(ne, dtype=np.float32)\n",
                "    ifl = 1 \n",
                "    \n",
                "    # Ensure types are correct for ctypes (float32 matches Fortran 'real' usually)\n",
                "    c_ear = energy_edges.astype(np.float32)\n",
                "    c_params = params.astype(np.float32)\n",
                "    c_ne = ct.c_int(ne)\n",
                "    c_ifl = ct.c_int(ifl)\n",
                "    \n",
                "    reltrans_pl_func(\n",
                "        c_ear.ctypes.data_as(type_float_p),\n",
                "        ct.byref(c_ne),\n",
                "        c_params.ctypes.data_as(type_float_p),\n",
                "        ct.byref(c_ifl),\n",
                "        photar.ctypes.data_as(type_float_p)\n",
                "    )\n",
                "    \n",
                "    return photar"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "markdown",
            "metadata": {},
            "source": [
                "## 3. Define Parameters and Grid\n",
                "\n",
                "We setup a standard energy grid (0.1 - 100 keV) and a baseline set of parameters."
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "code",
            "execution_count": null,
            "metadata": {},
            "outputs": [],
            "source": [
                "# Energy Grid\n",
                "n_bins = 200\n",
                "energy_edges = np.logspace(np.log10(0.1), np.log10(100.0), n_bins + 1)\n",
                "energy_centers = 0.5 * (energy_edges[1:] + energy_edges[:-1])\n",
                "\n",
                "# Parameter mapping for tdreltransPL:\n",
                "#  0: h1 (height 1)\n",
                "#  1: a (spin)\n",
                "#  2: inc (inclination)\n",
                "#  3: rin (inner radius, -1 for ISCO)\n",
                "#  4: rout (outer radius)\n",
                "#  5: zcos (redshift)\n",
                "#  6: Gamma (spectral index)\n",
                "#  7: logxi (ionization)\n",
                "#  8: Afe (Iron abundance)\n",
                "#  9: Ecut (High energy cutoff)\n",
                "# 10: Nh (Column density)\n",
                "# 11: boost\n",
                "# 12: Mass (Solar masses)\n",
                "# 13: floHz (Low freq, for timing)\n",
                "# 14: fhiHz (High freq, for timing)\n",
                "# 15: ReIm (1=Real, 2=Imag)\n",
                "# 16: DelA \n",
                "# 17: DelAB\n",
                "# 18: g\n",
                "# 19: telescope response\n",
                "\n",
                "default_params = [\n",
                "    10.0,  # h1\n",
                "    0.998, # a\n",
                "    30.0,  # inc\n",
                "    -1.0,  # rin\n",
                "    400.0, # rout\n",
                "    0.0,   # zcos\n",
                "    2.0,   # Gamma\n",
                "    3.0,   # logxi\n",
                "    1.0,   # Afe\n",
                "    300.0, # Ecut\n",
                "    0.0,   # Nh\n",
                "    1.0,   # boost\n",
                "    10.0,  # Mass\n",
                "    0.0,   # floHz\n",
                "    0.0,   # fhiHz\n",
                "    1.0,   # ReIm\n",
                "    0.0,   # DelA\n",
                "    0.0,   # DelAB\n",
                "    0.0,   # g\n",
                "    0.0,   # resp\n",
                "    0.0    # padding to match Fortran array size 21\n",
                "]\n",
                "\n",
                "params = np.array(default_params, dtype=np.float32)"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "markdown",
            "metadata": {},
            "source": [
                "## 4. Basic Spectrum Plot\n",
                "\n",
                "Let's run the model with the default parameters."
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "code",
            "execution_count": null,
            "metadata": {},
            "outputs": [],
            "source": [
                "try:\n",
                "    flux = run_reltrans_pl(energy_edges, params)\n",
                "    \n",
                "    plt.figure(figsize=(10, 6))\n",
                "    plt.loglog(energy_centers, flux)\n",
                "    plt.xlabel(\"Energy (keV)\")\n",
                "    plt.ylabel(\"Photon Flux\")\n",
                "    plt.title(\"Basic Reltrans Spectrum\")\n",
                "    plt.grid(True, which=\"both\", ls=\"-\", alpha=0.5)\n",
                "    plt.show()\n",
                "except Exception as e:\n",
                "    print(f\"Run failed: {e}\")\n",
                "    print(\"Ensure the library is loaded and compatible.\")"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "markdown",
            "metadata": {},
            "source": [
                "## 5. Parameter Sweep: Black Hole Spin ($a$)\n",
                "\n",
                "We vary the dimensionless spin parameter $a$ from 0 (non-rotating) to 0.998 (maximal rotation).  \n",
                "High spin allows the accretion disk to extend closer to the black hole, strengthening relativistic effects."
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "code",
            "execution_count": null,
            "metadata": {},
            "outputs": [],
            "source": [
                "spins = [0.0, 0.5, 0.9, 0.998]\n",
                "\n",
                "plt.figure(figsize=(10, 6))\n",
                "\n",
                "try:\n",
                "    for a in spins:\n",
                "        p = params.copy()\n",
                "        p[1] = a # Modify spin index\n",
                "        flux = run_reltrans_pl(energy_edges, p)\n",
                "        plt.loglog(energy_centers, flux, label=f\"a = {a}\")\n",
                "\n",
                "    plt.xlabel(\"Energy (keV)\")\n",
                "    plt.ylabel(\"Photon Flux\")\n",
                "    plt.title(\"Effect of Black Hole Spin\")\n",
                "    plt.legend()\n",
                "    plt.grid(True, which=\"both\", ls=\"-\", alpha=0.5)\n",
                "    plt.show()\n",
                "except Exception as e:\n",
                "    print(f\"Sweep failed: {e}\")"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "markdown",
            "metadata": {},
            "source": [
                "## 6. Parameter Sweep: Inclination Angle ($i$)\n",
                "\n",
                "We vary the inclination angle of the accretion disk relative to the observer line of sight.  \n",
                "Higher inclination leads to stronger Doppler boosting and structural changes in the line profile."
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "code",
            "execution_count": null,
            "metadata": {},
            "outputs": [],
            "source": [
                "incs = [20.0, 45.0, 60.0, 80.0]\n",
                "\n",
                "plt.figure(figsize=(10, 6))\n",
                "\n",
                "try:\n",
                "    for inc in incs:\n",
                "        p = params.copy()\n",
                "        p[2] = inc # Modify inclination index\n",
                "        flux = run_reltrans_pl(energy_edges, p)\n",
                "        plt.loglog(energy_centers, flux, label=f\"inc = {inc} deg\")\n",
                "\n",
                "    plt.xlabel(\"Energy (keV)\")\n",
                "    plt.ylabel(\"Photon Flux\")\n",
                "    plt.title(\"Effect of Inclination\")\n",
                "    plt.legend()\n",
                "    plt.grid(True, which=\"both\", ls=\"-\", alpha=0.5)\n",
                "    plt.show()\n",
                "except Exception as e:\n",
                "    print(f\"Sweep failed: {e}\")"
            ]
        }\n
    ],
